-- title:
--   Exact derivative rows for the normalized power 8
-- statement:
--   Set $m=8$, $a_m=23/2$, $b_m=253$. For fixed $m$, let $p_\beta(X)=(X^3-a_mX-b_m\beta)^m$. For every complex $\beta,z$ and each $m\le k<3m$, the stated explicit monic row polynomial is the normalized derivative
--
--   $$R_{m,k}(\beta,z)=\sum_{\substack{u+v+w=m\\3u+v\ge k}}\frac{m!}{u!v!w!}(-a_m)^v(-b_m\beta)^w\frac{(3u+v)!(3m-k)!}{(3u+v-k)!(3m)!}z^{3u+v-k},$$
--
--   where the summation indices are nonnegative integers, and $p_\beta^{(k)}(z)=(3m)!R_{m,k}(\beta,z)/(3m-k)!$. The formal packet lists each rational-coefficient expansion. The final three rows are $z^3-z-\beta$, $z^2-1/3$, and $z$. These are exact derivative identities supporting row selection.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/Amal-David/derivative-chain-prize/blob/21d2a2ac5cd4b4e6263cbc715dd5f925427fc976/continuation_formal/Source/EighthPowerRows.lean#L38-L65

